'''''Brugmansia'' × ''candida''''' (syn. ''Datura'' × ''candida''), also known as '''angel's trumpet''' or '''moonflower''',<ref name=":0">{{Cite book |last= |first= |title=A South African Garden for All Seasons; the Secrets of Year-Round Garden Beauty |last2= |first2= |publisher=Reader's Digest |pages=162}}</ref> is a hybrid species of flowering plant in the family [[Solanaceae]].<ref name="RHS_73486" >{{cite web |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/73486/brugmansia-candida/details73486 |title=''Brugmansia'' × ''candida'' |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2024 |website=Find a plant |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=24 September 2024}}</ref> Its parents are ''[[Brugmansia aurea]]'' and ''[[Brugmansia versicolor]]'', with both listed as [[extinct in the wild]].<ref name="POWO_814597-1" >{{cite POWO |id=814597-1 |title=''Brugmansia'' × ''candida'' Pers. |access-date=24 September 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite iucn |author=Hay, A. |year=2014 |title=''Brugmansia aurea'' |volume=2014 |article-number=e.T38124A58906215 |doi=10.2305/IUCN.UK.2014-1.RLTS.T38124A58906215.en |access-date=25 September 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite iucn |author=Hay, A. |year=2014 |title=''Brugmansia versicolor'' |volume=2014 |article-number=e.T38125A58908295 |doi=10.2305/IUCN.UK.2014-1.RLTS.T38125A58908295.en |access-date=25 September 2024}}</ref>

''Brugmansia'' × ''candida'' is native to Colombia and Ecuador, and has been introduced to tropical locations worldwide.<ref name="POWO_814597-1" /> A large shrub or small tree reaching at most {{cvt|6|m}}, it is typically found in the seasonally dry tropics.<ref name="RHS_73486" /> Its cultivars 'Angels Sunbeam', 'Creamsickle', 'Grand Marnier', and 'Knightii' have all gained the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]] as ornamentals.<ref name="RHS_AGM" >{{cite web |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/pdfs/agm-lists/agm-ornamentals.pdf |title=AGM Plants – ORNAMENTAL |date=April 2023 |page=15 |publisher=Royal Horticultural Society |website=www.rhs.org |access-date=24 September 2024}}</ref>

== Cultivation ==
It does best in warmer, frost-free regions. It should be watered regularly, especially in drier regions. Planted in well-drained, rich soil, in sunny or semi-shaded areas. In windy or colder regions, it is recommended to plant it in a sheltered space.<ref name=":0" />

